<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese money supply growth slows in April.</title>
<headline>Portuguese money supply growth slows in April.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese money supply, as measured by &quot;aggregate 'L&quot;, roughly equivalent to M3, rose 8.8 percent year-on-year in April, compared with growth of 9.6 percent in the previous month, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>Domestic bank lending grew 11.2 percent year-on-year in April, compared with 13.9 percent the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
